--[[
	Anomaly Coop - client guards for mod item paths that duplicate or lose items on a co-op client
	(gamedata\scripts\coop_mods_guard.script). B3 review round 1, Ruling L-2: until the id lease of F2 T12b a function a
	client cannot do safely is refused with a message rather than allowed to duplicate.

	On a client a world call is a request to the host (call router, F2 T12): alife():create and alife():register answer
	nil, alife():create(.., false) answers an unregistered entity (no id yet), alife_release only asks the host to remove
	(the item stays here until the host's EntityDestroy). A mod written for single player that indexes such a result
	between its create and its release stops on a Lua error (the router's pcall) with the create already sent:
	"created, never released". Every guard checks the role at call time (inert in single player and on the host, also
	after a disconnect) and is installed on a client only, at its first update, outermost: later wrappers (3DSS hooks at
	actor_on_first_update, Mags Redux at load) are wrapped again on the next check (once a second).

	C1  weapon variant swap (alife_clone_weapon: the scoped weapon is another section, GAMMA / 3DSS). _g_patches'
	    version registers the clone first and indexes register's answer (nil without an id) before it releases the old
	    weapon: each attach, detach, Toggle Scope key, magnifier switch or wheel scope change left the old weapon (and the
	    scope) beside the new one.
	    F2 T12b (leased ids): a client with ids (coop.lease_ids() >= SWAP_IDS) swaps a weapon in its own bag as in single
	    player - the clone is created here at once under a leased id, register answers it, the parts and m_data move to
	    its real id, and the old weapon's release goes with the clone (the host releases it when it creates the clone,
	    keeps it when it refuses). Without ids (right after joining), for a weapon outside the own bag or one that waits
	    for the host (its create or a clone of it not answered yet: round 1, review C1) the swap is refused on a client
	    before any world call, the player is told:
	      _G.alife_clone_weapon (backstop: magnifier fallback, MP-412 upgrade, any other caller)
	      item_weapon.attach_scope / detach_scope        a weapon with scope variants (parent_section); also Toggle
	                                                     Scope's override, canted irons' and battery hooks inside
	      utils_item.attach_addon / detach_addon         the scope-variant branch only (an engine addon is attached
	                                                     by the engine: silencers, launchers, engine scopes)
	      haru_quick_action_wheel_mcm.QScopeWheelOption  Attach / Detach without an engine scope
	    A magnifier in bone mode (3DSS, no clone) keeps working.
	I1  alife_create_item(.., own actor, {cond = x}) of a degradable item: the stock processor keeps x in a table under
	    the id register answers, which a client never gets, so the item came with condition 1 (a full battery, whole
	    canted irons). Here it goes as an unregistered entity with x written into it, then alife():register: the
	    request carries the entity's condition (coop_items.cpp capture_entity), the host applies it.
	C2  artefact containers (itms_manager.dropdrop_ArtyContainer / use_arty_container; zz_item_artefact replaces both
	    with versions that index the created container): run with deferred creates. alife_create_item into the own
	    actor answers an unregistered entity the mod can write (its condition), registered only after the function
	    returned, so its releases go first; a function that fails registers nothing.
	C3  keep-crafting-window mods (zz_item_cooking_ / zz_ui_workshop_keep_crafting_window_open): their refresh timers
	    are host-only (coop_compat_crafting.ltx): the ingredients just released are still in the local inventory until
	    the host confirms, a second action from them would be free. Until 2026-11-12 the window was closed after every
	    cook, craft, repair or upgrade on a client ("the workbench closes after every craft"). Now it stays open: the
	    next action is refused until the host has taken what this one released (or 5 s passed), then the mod's own
	    UpdateUi refreshes the window from the real inventory. The window still closes when the host does not answer
	    in 5 s or the refresh fails.
	I3  af_inspect (FDDA): inspect() locks the input until its temporary item arrives and is in slot 14; on a client
	    the lock is lifted after INSPECT_TIMEOUT_MS if it has not, the player is told, the item arriving later is
	    released. Its two level.add_call pairs are registered through a cancel switch: level.remove_call is not
	    reliable (stock _g.script, AddUniqueCall), and a pair left running would index the cleared item name in a
	    luabind functor (FATAL); cancelled, the condition answers true once and the action does nothing.
	I4  (round 2) the same for a random range, cond_r / cond_cr (mutant parts, loot): rolled with the processor's own
	    Random_Condition / Random_Choice as the host would (item_condition).
	C4  (round 2) crafting, cooking, repair and the melter from stashes (GAMMA's zzzzzz_*_nearby_stashes, the Hideout
	    Furniture workbench): the gate refuses the release of an item in a stash, the product came anyway. On a client
	    no stash is in range and the workshop gets no stash id: the backpack only, the player is told.
	I2  (part data and spawn budget of a swap) F2 T12b: the parts and m_data go to the clone's real id; the host charges
	    the budget only what the clone costs more than its source and creates it together with the source's release, so
	    a queue that drops it loses nothing.
	C5  item_weapon.ammo_aggregation of a box or a corpse (item_weapon's move, after an ammo pack is put there): the move waits for
	    the host, so a damaged pack is still ours here and its release goes out, the host allows it in the box, and the new pack
	    into the box is refused: the pack is gone. Merging packs there would change copies. A client sorts its own inventory only.
	C6  (2026-11-08, upgrade kits) the addon item_weapon.attach_scope uses up (a scope, a GAMMA upgrade kit) is released after
	    the host's Ok to the clone, kept and the player told on a refusal, and not fitted again while it waits.
	death_manager.decide_items_to_keep (xr_motivator, every dying NPC) stays on a client: its releases are refused, but its wear is
	all the weapon of the client's copy gets, it spawned whole and nothing else lowers it.
--]]

local api = rawget(_G, "coop")

local tostring, type, ipairs, pcall, select, unpack = tostring, type, ipairs, pcall, select, unpack

local function C() return coop_mods_core end
local function log(fmt, ...) C().log("guard", fmt, ...) end

-- The input lock of af_inspect: in single player it lasts the slot switch (hide the weapon, draw the item: about 1-2
-- s); a client adds the round trip of the item's request. 5 s covers a slow link and is short for a stuck player.
local INSPECT_TIMEOUT_MS = 5000
local INSPECT_LATE_MS = 30000 -- a temporary item arriving after the timeout is released for this long
local CHECK_MS = 1000         -- the guards are checked to be outermost
local TELL_GAP_MS = 2000      -- one message per id at most this often (a mouse wheel repeats the magnifier switch)
local MAX_REWRAPS = 8         -- per entry point: something that wraps it again and again is left alone (logged)

local TXT_SWAP = { "st_coop_guard_scope_swap",
	"Co-op: this scope change is not available on a client now (only for a weapon in your own backpack)." }
local TXT_INSPECT = { "st_coop_guard_inspect_timeout",
	"Co-op: the item to inspect did not come from the host, the inspection is cancelled." }
local TXT_FAILED = { "st_coop_guard_failed", "Co-op: this action could not be done on a client." }
local TXT_SETTLING = { "st_coop_guard_settling",
	"Co-op: wait a moment, the host is still taking the ingredients of the last action." }

stats = { refused = 0, swaps = 0, cond = 0, deferred = 0, failed = 0, closed = 0, kept = 0, settling_refused = 0,
	inspect_timeouts = 0, late_released = 0 }

local next_tell = {}
local function tell(txt)
	local now = time_global()
	if (next_tell[txt[1]] or 0) > now then return end
	next_tell[txt[1]] = now + TELL_GAP_MS
	C().hud(txt[1], txt[2])
end

-- results of pcall(f, ...) as a table with n
local function pack(...) return { n = select("#", ...), ... } end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Items and sections
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function section_of(obj)
	if type(obj) == "string" then return obj end
	local ok, s = pcall(function() return obj:section() end)
	return ok and type(s) == "string" and s or nil
end

local function section_exists(sec)
	if type(sec) ~= "string" then return false end
	local ok, e = pcall(function() return ini_sys:section_exist(sec) end)
	return ok and e == true
end

local function parent_section(sec)
	if type(sec) ~= "string" then return nil end
	local ok, p = pcall(function() return ini_sys:r_string_ex(sec, "parent_section") end)
	return ok and type(p) == "string" and p ~= "" and p or nil
end

-- a weapon whose scopes are other weapon sections: changing its scope clones it
local function variant_weapon(wpn) return parent_section(section_of(wpn)) ~= nil end

local function scoped_variant(wpn)
	local sec = section_of(wpn)
	local p = parent_section(sec)
	return p ~= nil and p ~= sec
end

local function engine_scope(wpn)
	local ok, name = pcall(function()
		local w = wpn:cast_Weapon()
		return w and w:GetScopeName()
	end)
	return ok and type(name) == "string" and name ~= ""
end

local function id_of(obj)
	local ok, id = pcall(function()
		if type(obj.id) == "function" then return obj:id() end
		return obj.id
	end)
	return ok and type(id) == "number" and id or nil
end

local function own_actor(owner)
	local a = db.actor
	if not (a and owner ~= nil) then return false end
	local id = id_of(owner)
	return id ~= nil and id == id_of(a)
end

local function degradable(sec)
	local ok, d = pcall(function()
		return utils_item.is_degradable(nil, sec) and not IsItem("multiuse", sec)
	end)
	return ok and d and true or false
end

-- An entity in the own actor that is not registered yet (alife():create(.., false); on a client F2 T12 keeps it until
-- alife():register sends it as a request).
local function unregistered(sec)
	local a = db.actor
	if not a then return nil end
	local ok, se = pcall(function()
		return alife():create(sec, a:position(), a:level_vertex_id(), a:game_vertex_id(), a:id(), false)
	end)
	return ok and se or nil
end

local function write_condition(se, cond)
	local ok, e = pcall(function()
		local data = utils_stpk.get_item_data(se)
		data.condition = clamp(cond, 0, 1)
		utils_stpk.set_item_data(data, se)
	end)
	if not ok then C().report("guard", "condition of " .. tostring(section_of(se) or "?"), e) end
end

-- alife():register's answer: on a client the item itself when it holds a leased id (F2 T12b), else nil (the item
-- comes with the host's answer).
local function register(se)
	local ok, r = pcall(function() return alife():register(se) end)
	if not ok then
		C().report("guard", "register", r)
		return nil
	end
	return r
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C1: weapon variant swap
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function refuse_swap()
	stats.refused = stats.refused + 1
	tell(TXT_SWAP)
end

-- F2 T12b: the ids a swap may take - the clone, a detached scope, one more for a later wrapper (canted irons give their
-- irons back first).
local SWAP_IDS = 3

local function lease_ids()
	local f = api and api.lease_ids
	if type(f) ~= "function" then return 0 end
	local ok, n = pcall(f)
	return ok and type(n) == "number" and n or 0
end

-- the holder's id of a server object (parent_id) or a game object (parent())
local function holder_id(obj)
	local ok, pid = pcall(function() return obj.parent_id end)
	if ok and type(pid) == "number" then return pid end
	ok, pid = pcall(function()
		local p = obj:parent()
		return p and p:id()
	end)
	return ok and type(pid) == "number" and pid or nil
end

-- the item `id` waits for the host: its create is not answered yet, or a clone of ours replaces it (coop.lease_waiting)
local function id_waiting(id)
	local f = api and api.lease_waiting
	if type(f) ~= "function" or id == nil then return false end
	local ok, w = pcall(f, id)
	return ok and w == true
end

-- F2 T12b round 1 (review C1): the weapon waits for the host - its create is not answered yet (the host's budget queue,
-- a retry), or a clone of ours replaces it already. The engine refuses its clone (nil), but the mods create the scope
-- before the clone (detach): refused here first, before any world call.
local function lease_waiting(wpn) return id_waiting(id_of(wpn)) end

-- A client clones its own weapon at once under a leased id: the weapon in its own bag (the clone goes where the weapon
-- is), ids enough for the swap, and a weapon the host has made already.
local function swap_ready(wpn, holder)
	local a = db.actor
	local pid = holder or holder_id(wpn)
	return C().live_client() and a ~= nil and pid ~= nil and pid == id_of(a) and lease_ids() >= SWAP_IDS
		and not lease_waiting(wpn)
end

-- when(...) -> the weapon the call would clone (nil: it clones nothing) and its holder's id when the call names it
local function swap_guard(when)
	return function(orig)
		return function(...)
			if C().is_client() then
				local wpn, holder = when(...)
				if wpn ~= nil then
					if not swap_ready(wpn, holder) then
						refuse_swap()
						return nil
					end
					stats.swaps = stats.swaps + 1
				end
			end
			return orig(...)
		end
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C6: the addon an attach uses up waits for the host's answer to the clone (2026-11-08)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Live report (GAMMA, stable 41.4): a client could not fit an upgrade kit (PP Vityaz), the host could. A kit is a
-- scope-style addon (mod_system_weapon_addons_upg_kits.ltx, 3DSS weapon_kit): item_weapon.attach_scope clones the weapon
-- into its variant (wpn_vityaz + vitup = wpn_vityaz_vitup) and then releases the kit. The engine refused that clone on a
-- client (fixed there: coop_id_lease.h addon_variant). Here: with leased ids the clone is made at once and its create
-- waits for the host, while the addon's release went out at once, so a clone the host refused (its budget queue full,
-- the weapon not his there) left the weapon as it was and took the addon - a kit costs up to 88 000. Now the addon's
-- release waits for that answer: the host's Ok (the weapon the clone replaces is gone here) releases it, a refusal (the
-- clone taken back here) keeps it and tells the player. Until then that addon cannot be fitted again (one kit, two
-- weapons). Scopes go the same way.
local NO_ID = 65535
-- an answered clone whose old weapon stays here (its destroy failed on the host) uses the addon up after this: the
-- clone is ours, a kept addon would be a second one
local FIT_WAIT_MS = 60000
local TXT_FIT_WAIT = { "st_coop_guard_fit_wait", "Co-op: this addon is being fitted, wait for the host's answer." }
local TXT_FIT_REFUSED = { "st_coop_guard_fit_refused",
	"Co-op: the host did not accept the change, the weapon is as it was and the addon stays with you." }
stats.fits, stats.fits_done, stats.fits_refused, stats.fit_waits = 0, 0, 0, 0
local fits = {} -- addon id -> { clone = id, source = id, at = ms, sec = the addon's section }

-- true / false; nil when this machine cannot tell (no ALife now)
local function in_world(id)
	local ok, se = pcall(function() return alife():object(id) end)
	if not ok then return nil end
	return se ~= nil
end

local function release_fitted(id, f)
	local ok, e = pcall(function()
		local se = alife():object(id)
		if se then alife_release(se) end
	end)
	if not ok then C().report("guard", "release of the fitted " .. f.sec, e) end
end

local function fit_tick(now)
	if next(fits) == nil then return end
	for id, f in pairs(fits) do
		if not id_waiting(f.clone) then
			-- the old weapon first: the host releases it only with the clone it made, which may be gone already (a sight
			-- on it at once: replaced by its own clone)
			local source_here, clone_here = in_world(f.source), in_world(f.clone)
			if source_here == false or (clone_here == true and now - f.at >= FIT_WAIT_MS) then
				fits[id] = nil
				stats.fits_done = stats.fits_done + 1
				release_fitted(id, f)
			elseif source_here == true and clone_here == false then
				fits[id] = nil
				stats.fits_refused = stats.fits_refused + 1
				log("%s %d stays: the host refused the weapon's new variant %d (the engine took it back)", f.sec, id, f.clone)
				tell(TXT_FIT_REFUSED)
			end
		end
	end
end

-- attach_scope with the addon's release held when the call made a clone of ours (a client: the clone has its leased id)
local function fit_after_answer(orig)
	return function(item, weapon, ...)
		if not C().is_client() then return orig(item, weapon, ...) end
		local addon = id_of(item)
		if addon ~= nil and fits[addon] then
			stats.fit_waits = stats.fit_waits + 1
			tell(TXT_FIT_WAIT)
			return nil
		end
		local real_clone, real_release = rawget(_G, "alife_clone_weapon"), rawget(_G, "alife_release")
		if not (C().live_client() and addon ~= nil and type(real_clone) == "function" and type(real_release) == "function") then
			return orig(item, weapon, ...)
		end
		local made, held
		rawset(_G, "alife_clone_weapon", function(se, ...)
			local new = real_clone(se, ...)
			local id = new ~= nil and id_of(new) or nil
			local source = id_of(se)
			if made == nil and id ~= nil and id ~= NO_ID and source ~= nil then made = { clone = id, source = source } end
			return new
		end)
		rawset(_G, "alife_release", function(obj, ...)
			if made ~= nil and not held and id_of(obj) == addon then
				held = true -- released by fit_tick after the host's answer
				return
			end
			return real_release(obj, ...)
		end)
		local res = pack(pcall(orig, item, weapon, ...))
		rawset(_G, "alife_clone_weapon", real_clone)
		rawset(_G, "alife_release", real_release)
		if held then
			fits[addon] = { clone = made.clone, source = made.source, at = time_global(), sec = section_of(item) or "addon" }
			stats.fits = stats.fits + 1
		end
		if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
		return unpack(res, 2, res.n)
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- I1 / C2: creates into the own actor
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- I4 (B3 round 2): the condition ItemProcessor:Create_Item gives an item: t.cond, or a roll from t.cond_r (t.cond_cr
-- for items of type cond_ct) with the processor's own Random_Condition ({a, b}: random(a, b) / 100) or Random_Choice
-- (more than two values). The processor tests IsItem(cond_ct, section) with a GLOBAL cond_ct (a typo for t.cond_ct in
-- 1.5.3 and GAMMA), so its cond_cr branch never runs; the same lookup here gives what the host would give. Mutant
-- parts (ui_mutant_loot, death_manager: cond_r = {30, 70}) came to a client with condition 1.
local function processor_roll(list)
	local m = rawget(_G, "itms_manager")
	local ok, v = pcall(function()
		local p = m and m.get_item_processor and m.get_item_processor()
		if not p then return nil end
		if #list > 2 then return p:Random_Choice(list) end
		return p:Random_Condition(list)
	end)
	if ok and type(v) == "number" then return v end
	if #list > 2 then return list[math.random(1, #list)] end
	if #list == 2 and type(list[1]) == "number" and type(list[2]) == "number" then
		return math.random(list[1], list[2]) / 100
	end
	return nil
end

local function item_condition(section, t)
	local cond = t.cond
	local m = rawget(_G, "itms_manager")
	local ct = type(m) == "table" and rawget(m, "cond_ct") or nil
	if ct == nil then ct = rawget(_G, "cond_ct") end
	if type(t.cond_cr) == "table" and t.cond_ct and ct ~= nil and IsItem(ct, section) then
		cond = processor_roll(t.cond_cr)
	elseif type(t.cond_r) == "table" then
		cond = processor_roll(t.cond_r)
	end
	return type(cond) == "number" and cond or nil
end

local function cond_create(orig)
	return function(section, owner, t, ...)
		local cond = C().live_client() and type(t) == "table" and t.ammo == nil and t.uses == nil
			and section_exists(section) and own_actor(owner) and degradable(section) and item_condition(section, t)
		if cond then
			local se = unregistered(section)
			if se then
				write_condition(se, cond)
				stats.cond = stats.cond + 1
				-- F2 T12b: the item itself with a leased id; nil without one (it comes with the host's answer)
				return register(se)
			end
		end
		return orig(section, owner, t, ...)
	end
end

local function with_deferred_creates(label, f, ...)
	local real = rawget(_G, "alife_create_item")
	if type(real) ~= "function" then return f(...) end
	local made = {}
	rawset(_G, "alife_create_item", function(section, owner, t, ...)
		if section_exists(section) and own_actor(owner) then
			local se = unregistered(section)
			if se then
				if type(t) == "table" and type(t.cond) == "number" then write_condition(se, t.cond) end
				made[#made + 1] = se
				return se
			end
		end
		return real(section, owner, t, ...)
	end)
	local res = pack(pcall(f, ...))
	rawset(_G, "alife_create_item", real)
	if not res[1] then
		-- nothing created: what it released before the error is lost, never doubled
		stats.failed = stats.failed + 1
		C().report("guard", label, res[2])
		tell(TXT_FAILED)
		return nil
	end
	for _, se in ipairs(made) do register(se) end
	stats.deferred = stats.deferred + #made
	return unpack(res, 2, res.n)
end

local function deferred(label)
	return function(orig)
		return function(...)
			if not C().live_client() then return orig(...) end
			return with_deferred_creates(label, orig, ...)
		end
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C3: crafting windows on a client stay open and wait for the host
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A release on a client is a request: the ingredient stays in the local inventory until the destroy of the host
-- comes back. A second action from it found nothing to release and created the product again (free). So while the
-- items an action released are still here, every guarded action (any window, any tab) is refused and the player is
-- told; when they are gone, and the products the action asked for have come into the inventory (or PRODUCT_MS
-- passed: a product made into a stash never comes), the UpdateUi of the mod refreshes the window, which stayed
-- open. What the action released, created and used up is seen by standing in front of the stock helpers for the
-- length of the call (the mods call them as globals).
local SETTLE_MIN_MS = 100  -- the refresh delay of the mods themselves
local SETTLE_MAX_MS = 5000 -- the host has not taken the ingredients (refused, a dead link): the window closes
local PRODUCT_MS = 1500    -- the ingredients are gone, the product is waited for this long

local settling = nil -- the one action being settled: { ids, creates, takes0, since, deadline, self, window, gone_at }
local takes = 0      -- items that came into the own inventory (actor_on_item_take)

local function id_of(x)
	if type(x) == "number" then return x end
	local ok, id = pcall(function()
		if type(x.id) == "number" then return x.id end
		return x:id()
	end)
	return ok and type(id) == "number" and id or nil
end

local function here(id)
	local ok, o = pcall(level.object_by_id, id)
	return ok and o ~= nil
end

-- Runs f(self, ...) and answers pack(pcall(..)) and what it released (ids), asked to create into the own actor and
-- discharged.
local function watched(f, self, ...)
	local rec = { ids = {}, n = 0, creates = 0, uses = 0 }
	local function note(x)
		local id = id_of(x)
		if id and not rec.ids[id] then rec.ids[id], rec.n = true, rec.n + 1 end
	end
	local me = id_of(db.actor)
	local rel, rel_id, create = rawget(_G, "alife_release"), rawget(_G, "alife_release_id"), rawget(_G, "alife_create_item")
	local items = rawget(_G, "utils_item")
	local discharge = type(items) == "table" and items.discharge or nil
	if type(rel) == "function" then
		rawset(_G, "alife_release", function(x, ...) note(x); return rel(x, ...) end)
	end
	if type(rel_id) == "function" then
		rawset(_G, "alife_release_id", function(x, ...) note(x); return rel_id(x, ...) end)
	end
	if type(create) == "function" then
		rawset(_G, "alife_create_item", function(sec, parent, ...)
			if me ~= nil and id_of(parent) == me then rec.creates = rec.creates + 1 end
			return create(sec, parent, ...)
		end)
	end
	if type(discharge) == "function" then
		items.discharge = function(...) rec.uses = rec.uses + 1; return discharge(...) end
	end
	local res = pack(pcall(f, self, ...))
	if type(rel) == "function" then rawset(_G, "alife_release", rel) end
	if type(rel_id) == "function" then rawset(_G, "alife_release_id", rel_id) end
	if type(create) == "function" then rawset(_G, "alife_create_item", create) end
	if type(discharge) == "function" then items.discharge = discharge end
	return res, rec
end

local function settle_after(window_of)
	return function(orig)
		return function(self, ...)
			if not C().is_client() then return orig(self, ...) end
			if settling then
				stats.settling_refused = stats.settling_refused + 1
				tell(TXT_SETTLING)
				return
			end
			local res, rec = watched(orig, self, ...)
			if rec.n > 0 or rec.creates > 0 or rec.uses > 0 then -- it did something: an action that returned at once leaves no trace
				local now = time_global()
				local okw, win = pcall(window_of, self)
				settling = { ids = rec.ids, creates = rec.creates, takes0 = takes, since = now, deadline = now + SETTLE_MAX_MS,
					self = self, window = okw and win or nil }
			end
			if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
			return unpack(res, 2, res.n)
		end
	end
end

local function settling_shown(s)
	if not s.window then return false end
	local ok, shown = pcall(function() return s.window:IsShown() end)
	return ok and shown == true
end

local function settling_close(s)
	stats.closed = stats.closed + 1
	local ok, e = pcall(function() s.self:Close() end)
	if not ok then C().report("guard", "close the crafting window", e) end
end

local function settle_tick(now)
	local s = settling
	if not s then return end
	for id in pairs(s.ids) do
		if not here(id) then s.ids[id] = nil end
	end
	if next(s.ids) ~= nil then
		if now < s.deadline then return end
		settling = nil -- as before this guard kept the window: it closes, the next action is up to the player
		log("the host did not take the ingredients of a crafting action in %d ms: the window is closed", SETTLE_MAX_MS)
		if settling_shown(s) then settling_close(s) end
		return
	end
	if now < s.since + SETTLE_MIN_MS then return end
	s.gone_at = s.gone_at or now
	if s.creates > 0 and takes - s.takes0 < s.creates and now < s.gone_at + PRODUCT_MS then return end
	settling = nil
	if not settling_shown(s) then return end -- the stock window closed itself, or the player closed it
	if s.self.last_cont == nil or s.self.last_idx == nil then return end -- the mods refresh only with a selection
	stats.kept = stats.kept + 1
	local ok, e = pcall(function()
		if type(s.self.UpdateUi) ~= "function" then error("the window has no UpdateUi", 0) end
		return s.self:UpdateUi(s.self.last_cont, s.self.last_idx)
	end)
	if not ok then
		C().report("guard", "refresh the crafting window", e)
		settling_close(s)
	end
end

local function the_window(self) return self end
local function its_owner(self) return self.owner end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- I3: af_inspect input lock
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local watch -- { deadline, ticket = { cancelled, n }, item }
local late  -- { item, deadline }

local function inspect_guard(orig)
	return function(...)
		if not C().is_client() then return orig(...) end
		local ticket = { cancelled = false, n = 0 }
		local lvl = level
		local real_add = lvl.add_call
		-- add_call is overloaded in the engine (2 or 3 arguments): anything but (condition, action) goes as it is
		lvl.add_call = function(...)
			if select("#", ...) == 2 then
				local c, a = ...
				if type(c) == "function" and type(a) == "function" then
					ticket.n = ticket.n + 1
					return real_add(function()
						if ticket.cancelled then return true end
						return c()
					end, function()
						if not ticket.cancelled then return a() end
					end)
				end
			end
			return real_add(...)
		end
		local res = pack(pcall(orig, ...))
		lvl.add_call = real_add
		local m = rawget(_G, "af_inspect")
		if res[1] and type(m) == "table" and m.af_anim_item ~= nil and ticket.n > 0 then
			watch = { deadline = time_global() + INSPECT_TIMEOUT_MS, ticket = ticket, item = "tch_" .. tostring(m.af_anim_item) }
		end
		if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
		return unpack(res, 2, res.n)
	end
end

local function active_slot()
	local ok, s = pcall(function() return db.actor:active_slot() end)
	return ok and s or nil
end

local function inspect_tick(now)
	local m = rawget(_G, "af_inspect")
	if watch then
		if type(m) ~= "table" or m.af_anim_item == nil or active_slot() == 14 then
			watch = nil -- the item came (the mod gave the input back) or the inspection ended
		elseif now >= watch.deadline then
			watch.ticket.cancelled = true
			pcall(level.enable_input)
			m.af_anim_item, m.active_slot = nil, nil
			stats.inspect_timeouts = stats.inspect_timeouts + 1
			log("af_inspect: %s did not arrive in %d ms, the input is back", watch.item, INSPECT_TIMEOUT_MS)
			tell(TXT_INSPECT)
			late = { item = watch.item, deadline = now + INSPECT_LATE_MS }
			watch = nil
		end
	end
	if late then
		local ok, obj = pcall(function() return db.actor:object(late.item) end)
		if ok and obj then
			local okr, e = pcall(alife_release, obj)
			if okr then stats.late_released = stats.late_released + 1 else C().report("guard", "late af_inspect item", e) end
			late = nil
		elseif now >= late.deadline then
			late = nil
		end
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C5: a client's copy leaves these alone
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function own_ammo_only(orig)
	return function(obj, npc, ...)
		if C().is_client() and npc ~= nil and npc:id() ~= db.actor:id() then return true end
		return orig(obj, npc, ...)
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entry points, kept outermost
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function module_of(name) return function() return C().mod(name) end end
local function class_of(name, cls)
	return function()
		local m = C().mod(name)
		local ok, c = pcall(function() return m and m[cls] end)
		return ok and c or nil
	end
end

local function pending_mutation(orig)
	return function(obj, ...)
		local id = type(obj) == "number" and obj or id_of(obj)
		if C().is_client() and id ~= nil and id_waiting(id) then refuse_swap() return nil end
		return orig(obj, ...)
	end
end

local GUARDS = {
	{ label = "zzzz_arti_jamming_repairs.replace_part", tbl = module_of("zzzz_arti_jamming_repairs"), key = "replace_part", make = pending_mutation },
	{ label = "zzzz_arti_jamming_repairs.act_fieldstrip", tbl = module_of("zzzz_arti_jamming_repairs"), key = "act_fieldstrip", make = pending_mutation },
	{ label = "item_parts.func_disassembly", tbl = module_of("item_parts"), key = "func_disassembly", make = pending_mutation },
	{ label = "item_parts.disassembly_weapon", tbl = module_of("item_parts"), key = "disassembly_weapon", make = pending_mutation },
	{ label = "_G.alife_clone_weapon", tbl = function() return _G end, key = "alife_clone_weapon",
		make = swap_guard(function(se, section, parent_id) return se, parent_id end) },
	{ label = "item_weapon.attach_scope", tbl = module_of("item_weapon"), key = "attach_scope",
		make = function(orig)
			return fit_after_answer(swap_guard(function(item, weapon)
				if item ~= nil and weapon ~= nil and variant_weapon(weapon) then return weapon end
			end)(orig))
		end },
	{ label = "item_weapon.detach_scope", tbl = module_of("item_weapon"), key = "detach_scope",
		make = swap_guard(function(weapon)
			if weapon ~= nil and scoped_variant(weapon) then return weapon end
		end) },
	{ label = "utils_item.attach_addon", tbl = module_of("utils_item"), key = "attach_addon",
		make = swap_guard(function(wpn, addon, typ)
			local ws, as = section_of(wpn), section_of(addon)
			if typ == "scope" and ws ~= nil and as ~= nil and section_exists(ws .. "_" .. as) then return wpn end
		end) },
	{ label = "utils_item.detach_addon", tbl = module_of("utils_item"), key = "detach_addon",
		make = swap_guard(function(wpn, addon, typ)
			if typ == "scope" and wpn ~= nil and scoped_variant(wpn) then
				-- a gun in a box or a body: coop_mods_items takes it into the bag first and runs the detach there, through
				-- the guard's inner copies (the swap is checked on the taken gun)
				local it = C().mod("coop_mods_items")
				local ok, takes = pcall(function() return it and it.takes_first and it.takes_first(wpn) end)
				if ok and takes == true then return nil end
				return wpn
			end
		end) },
	{ label = "QScopeWheelOption.Attach", tbl = class_of("haru_quick_action_wheel_mcm", "QScopeWheelOption"),
		key = "Attach",
		make = swap_guard(function(self, obj, wpn)
			if wpn ~= nil and not engine_scope(wpn) and variant_weapon(wpn) then return wpn end
		end) },
	{ label = "QScopeWheelOption.Detach", tbl = class_of("haru_quick_action_wheel_mcm", "QScopeWheelOption"),
		key = "Detach",
		make = swap_guard(function(self, wpn)
			if wpn ~= nil and not engine_scope(wpn) and scoped_variant(wpn) then return wpn end
		end) },
	{ label = "itms_manager.create_item", tbl = module_of("itms_manager"), key = "create_item", make = cond_create },
	{ label = "itms_manager.dropdrop_ArtyContainer", tbl = module_of("itms_manager"), key = "dropdrop_ArtyContainer",
		make = deferred("artefact into a container") },
	{ label = "itms_manager.use_arty_container", tbl = module_of("itms_manager"), key = "use_arty_container",
		make = deferred("artefact out of a container") },
	{ label = "item_cooking.UICook.OnCook", tbl = class_of("item_cooking", "UICook"), key = "OnCook",
		make = settle_after(the_window) },
	{ label = "ui_workshop.UIWorkshopCraft.Craft", tbl = class_of("ui_workshop", "UIWorkshopCraft"), key = "Craft",
		make = settle_after(its_owner) },
	{ label = "ui_workshop.UIWorkshopRepair.Repair", tbl = class_of("ui_workshop", "UIWorkshopRepair"), key = "Repair",
		make = settle_after(its_owner) },
	{ label = "ui_workshop.UIWorkshopUpgrade.Upgrade", tbl = class_of("ui_workshop", "UIWorkshopUpgrade"),
		key = "Upgrade", make = settle_after(its_owner) },
	{ label = "af_inspect.inspect", tbl = module_of("af_inspect"), key = "inspect", make = inspect_guard },
	{ label = "item_weapon.ammo_aggregation", tbl = module_of("item_weapon"), key = "ammo_aggregation", make = own_ammo_only },
}
for _, g in ipairs(GUARDS) do g.n = 0 end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C4 (B3 round 2): crafting, cooking, repair and the melter from stashes
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- GAMMA's "craft from nearby stashes" family takes ingredients from stashes: zzzzzz_ui_workshop_nearby_stashes defines
-- _G.GetStashesInRange / IterateStashesInRange / collect_amount_in_range, which zzzzzz_craft_use_low_cond_,
-- zzzzzz_item_cooking_, zzzzzz_item_repair_ and zzzzzz_grok_artefacts_melter_nearby_stashes use; the Hideout
-- Furniture workbench opens the workshop with its stash (stashId, read by GAMMA's ui_workshop and craft_use_low_cond;
-- coop_mods_hf opens it with the host's box on a client). On a client the release, discharge or uses change of an
-- item in a stash is refused by the call gate (not ours: own_release) and only logged, while the product is created:
-- free crafting, endless. Until a stash item can go into the bag first (transfer_item, F2 T12b) a client crafts,
-- cooks and repairs from its backpack only and is told so: no stash is in range, the workshop gets no stash id.
local STASH_TELL_GAP_MS = 30000 -- the lists ask for the stashes on every refresh
local TXT_STASH = { "st_coop_guard_stash",
	"Co-op: on a client crafting, cooking and repair take items from your backpack only (stashes are not available yet)." }
stats.stashes = 0
local next_stash_tell = 0

local function tell_stash()
	stats.stashes = stats.stashes + 1
	local now = time_global()
	if now < next_stash_tell then return end
	next_stash_tell = now + STASH_TELL_GAP_MS
	log("stash ingredients refused on a client: the backpack only (#%d)", stats.stashes)
	C().hud(TXT_STASH[1], TXT_STASH[2])
end

local function no_stashes(orig)
	return function(...)
		if not C().is_client() then return orig(...) end
		local ok, found = pcall(orig, ...)
		if ok and type(found) == "table" and next(found) ~= nil then tell_stash() end
		return {}
	end
end

-- argument #index of the function is a stash id: dropped on a client
local function no_stash_arg(index)
	return function(orig)
		return function(...)
			if not C().is_client() then return orig(...) end
			local args = pack(...)
			if args[index] ~= nil then
				args[index] = nil
				tell_stash()
			end
			return orig(unpack(args, 1, args.n))
		end
	end
end

local STASH_GUARDS = {
	{ label = "_G.GetStashesInRange", tbl = function() return _G end, key = "GetStashesInRange", make = no_stashes },
	{ label = "_G.collect_amount_in_range", tbl = function() return _G end, key = "collect_amount_in_range",
		make = no_stash_arg(3) },
	{ label = "ui_furniture_workshop.OpenWorkshop", tbl = module_of("ui_furniture_workshop"), key = "OpenWorkshop",
		make = no_stash_arg(1) },
	{ label = "ui_workshop.get_workshop_ui", tbl = module_of("ui_workshop"), key = "get_workshop_ui",
		make = no_stash_arg(5) },
}
for _, g in ipairs(STASH_GUARDS) do
	g.n = 0
	GUARDS[#GUARDS + 1] = g
end

local function current(tbl, key)
	if tbl == _G then
		local f = rawget(_G, key)
		return type(f) == "function" and f or nil
	end
	return C().fn(tbl, key)
end

local function ensure(g)
	local ok, tbl = pcall(g.tbl)
	if not (ok and tbl) then return end
	local cur = current(tbl, g.key)
	if not cur or cur == g.fn then return end
	if g.n >= MAX_REWRAPS then
		if not g.gave_up then
			g.gave_up = true
			log("! %s keeps being replaced, left as it is after %d wraps", g.label, g.n)
		end
		return
	end
	local w = g.make(cur)
	local okw, e = pcall(function() tbl[g.key] = w end)
	if not okw then
		C().report("guard", "wrap " .. g.label, e)
		return
	end
	g.fn = w
	g.n = g.n + 1
	if g.n == 1 then
		local list = C().wrapped
		if type(list) == "table" then list[#list + 1] = g.label end
	else
		log("%s was wrapped by a later script: the guard is outermost again (#%d)", g.label, g.n)
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- T1 GAMMA's craft tooltip before the world (every role and single player, inert where the mod is absent)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- zzz_craft_use_in_tooltip_mcm replaces utils_ui.UIInfoItem.Update at its load (:182) with one that reads craft.ltx and
-- cook.ltx through its file locals ini_craft / ini_cook (:2-3), opened only in its on_game_start (:476-477). A tooltip
-- shown before that (the main-menu new-game windows: stock ui_mm_faction_select's loadout, the co-op character window)
-- failed on every hover: ":288: attempt to index upvalue 'ini_craft' (a nil value)" (reports b40-b43). The two locals
-- are filled with the very files its on_game_start opens, once, when they are still nil; its on_game_start later
-- assigns its own (the same files).
local CRAFT_TIP_MOD = "zzz_craft_use_in_tooltip_mcm"
local CRAFT_TIP_INI = {
	{ fn = "getCraftableItems", up = "ini_craft", file = "items\\settings\\craft.ltx" },
	{ fn = "getCookableItems", up = "ini_cook", file = "items\\settings\\cook.ltx" },
}

local function fill_ini_upvalue(f, name, file)
	for i = 1, 255 do
		local n, v = debug.getupvalue(f, i)
		if n == nil then return end
		if n == name then
			if v == nil then debug.setupvalue(f, i, ini_file(file)) end
			return
		end
	end
end

function craft_tooltip_ready()
	local m = rawget(_G, CRAFT_TIP_MOD)
	if type(m) ~= "table" then return end
	for _, u in ipairs(CRAFT_TIP_INI) do
		local f = rawget(m, u.fn)
		if type(f) == "function" then
			local ok, err = pcall(fill_ini_upvalue, f, u.up, u.file)
			if not ok then printf("! [coop_mods_guard] craft tooltip %s: %s", u.up, tostring(err)) end
		end
	end
end

-- Wraps UIInfoItem.Update once per Lua state. Either order works: wrapped after the mod, this runs first; wrapped
-- before it, the mod's Update calls the function it replaced (og_info_item_update, :184) before it reads the files.
local craft_tip_wrapper = nil
local function install_craft_tooltip()
	if craft_tip_wrapper then return end
	local ok, ui = pcall(function() return utils_ui end)
	local cls = ok and type(ui) == "table" and ui.UIInfoItem
	local prev = type(cls) == "table" and cls.Update
	if type(prev) ~= "function" then return end
	craft_tip_wrapper = function(self, ...)
		craft_tooltip_ready()
		return prev(self, ...)
	end
	cls.Update = craft_tip_wrapper
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Start, status
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local next_check = 0

local function actor_on_update()
	if not C().is_client() then return end
	local now = time_global()
	inspect_tick(now)
	fit_tick(now)
	settle_tick(now)
	if now < next_check then return end
	next_check = now + CHECK_MS
	for _, g in ipairs(GUARDS) do ensure(g) end
end

local function status()
	local on = {}
	for _, g in ipairs(GUARDS) do
		if g.n > 0 then on[#on + 1] = g.label .. (g.n > 1 and ("x" .. g.n) or "") end
	end
	return string.format("scope swaps refused %d, done with leased ids %d (%d ids now), addons used up after the host's "
		.. "answer %d (used up %d, kept on a refusal %d, refits refused %d), conditions carried %d, "
		.. "container creates deferred %d (failed %d), crafting windows kept open %d (closed %d, actions refused while "
		.. "the host was taking the ingredients %d), af_inspect timeouts %d (late items "
		.. "released %d) | guarding: %s",
		stats.refused, stats.swaps, lease_ids(), stats.fits, stats.fits_done, stats.fits_refused, stats.fit_waits, stats.cond,
		stats.deferred, stats.failed, stats.kept, stats.closed, stats.settling_refused, stats.inspect_timeouts,
		stats.late_released, #on > 0 and table.concat(on, ", ") or "nothing yet (a client installs at its first update)")
end

-- on_game_start must not throw (axr_main runs every script's on_game_start in one unprotected loop, W5)
function on_game_start()
	if not api then return end
	local ok, e = pcall(function()
		install_craft_tooltip()
		RegisterScriptCallback("actor_on_update", actor_on_update)
		RegisterScriptCallback("actor_on_item_take", function() takes = takes + 1 end) -- C3: the product of a craft came
		C().status_line("guard", status)
	end)
	if not ok then printf("! [coop_mods_guard] start failed: %s", tostring(e)) end
end

-- at load as well: a window before the world (main menu) gets no on_game_start
if api then pcall(install_craft_tooltip) end
